# Hardening watch orchestrator — OPTIONAL agent-invocation config.
#
# Copy to `scripts/hardening-watch.env` (gitignored) to let the watcher AUTO-INVOKE the next
# agent in --run-once / --interval. If unset, the watcher runs supervised MANUAL mode: it tells
# you which agent + packet to run, you run it, then re-run the watcher. Both are valid.
#
# Templates support placeholders: {{TASK_FILE}} {{AGENT}} {{WAVE}}
# The command MUST: read the packet, do the work, COMMIT (docs/approved scope), and UPDATE the
# handoff files (flip next_agent, append AGENT_HANDOFF_LOG, write the next packet). The watcher
# validates afterwards (new commit, clean tree, diff within allowed paths, handoff updated) and
# REJECTS the result if the agent didn't complete the handoff (exit 6).
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENVIRONMENT NOTE (checked 2026-06-29): NO agent CLI is installed on this machine.
# Install + authenticate one before these will work. Verify the binary is on PATH (`which …`).
# A wrong/missing command now fails cleanly (exit 5, state preserved) — it does NOT strand the
# loop at a Sam gate. Always prove with a supervised --run-once before --interval; never overnight.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Option 1 (recommended): Claude Code headless for BOTH roles (Anthropic-native, one tool) ──
# Install:  curl -fsSL https://claude.ai/install.sh | bash
# Auth:     claude setup-token   → export CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=...   (or export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...)
# Verify:   which claude && claude --version
# Then set BOTH (acceptEdits lets it edit; allow only the git/test tools it needs — NOT --dangerously-skip-permissions):
# HARDENING_CURSOR_CMD=claude -p "$(cat {{TASK_FILE}})" --permission-mode acceptEdits --allowedTools "Read,Edit,Write,Bash(git add *),Bash(git commit *),Bash(npm run lint)"
# HARDENING_CLAUDE_CMD=claude -p "$(cat {{TASK_FILE}})" --permission-mode acceptEdits --allowedTools "Read,Edit,Write,Bash(git add *),Bash(git commit *),Bash(npm run lint)"

# ── Option 2: Cursor agent CLI for the execute role (if you specifically want Cursor) ──
# Install:  curl https://cursor.com/install -fsS | bash      (adds ~/.local/bin to PATH)
# Verify:   which cursor-agent && cursor-agent --version
# Headless form is `-p "<prompt>" --force` (NOT `--file`). Known gotcha: `-p` can hang / not
# release the terminal in some versions — test before trusting in a loop.
# HARDENING_CURSOR_CMD=cursor-agent -p "$(cat {{TASK_FILE}})" --force --output-format text
